  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-13T15:58:54.913Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Creating a world portal with a roomId containing a valid worldId but with unexpected whitespace characters (space, newline, etc) appended or prepended causes the portal to create a \"403 - Forbidden\" error popup and then become non-interactable after one use. Visually, however, the portal displays the world correctly. \n\nWhen trying to use such a portal, the log indicates that the client tries to fetch a destination of \"worldid:worldid\", instead of \"worldid:instanceid\" as it's supposed to. Sometimes, a few seconds after using the portal you can also get an \"Unusual Client Behaviour\" popup, followed by a disconnect from the instance. So far I've only seen it happen to people in VR, but it happens with random frequency so it's difficult to test.\n\nI've created a test world that has different combinations of whitespace characters appended to the roomId of portals, as well as some other things like ownership transfer on portal refresh to test whether ownership is involved with the disconnect. To use, pick a test from #2-#7 (#1 is a regular portal with nothing altered) & hit the \"Refresh Portal\" button, then attempt to use the portal. \n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_6dae494a-be77-4d63-9309-f28c22b708ce",
